    "topic_id": 38399,
    "poster_id": 1991,
    "post_rendered": "For a fixed <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e05fb47730e61c3f82e2a75dd4a0a7d295ff7ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta \\in \\lbrack 0, \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\rbrack$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"71\" height=\"33\" >,</span> find the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/5/20589a7e8c626cf6e1e91120aee205cd95a3bde6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\in \\mathbb{R}^{+}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" > which satisfies the following conditions:<br>\n<br>\n<b>I. </b> <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/a/b6a09e55a7baf1a1e5aca812ef5f8cc5d764bf24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt a}{\\cos \\theta} + \\frac{\\sqrt a}{\\sin \\theta} &gt;\n1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"133\" height=\"39\" >.</span><br>\n<br>\n<b>II.</b> There exists <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/5/595f8b4dd1db2904da02ed1a081610835b5695ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in \\lbrack 1 - \\frac{\\sqrt a}{\\sin \\theta},\n\\frac{\\sqrt a}{\\cos \\theta} \\rbrack$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"159\" height=\"39\" > such that <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d4766eca04fb860fc1d38061c89b3618f10b7d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lbrack (1 -\nx)\\sin \\theta - \\sqrt{a - x^2 \\cos^{2} \\theta} \\rbrack^{2} +\n\\lbrack x\\cos \\theta - \\sqrt{a - (1 - x)^2 \\sin^{2} \\theta}\n\\rbrack^{2} \\leq a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"548\" height=\"32\" >.</span>",
    "post_canonical": "For a fixed $\\theta \\in \\lbrack 0, \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\rbrack$, find the smallest $a \\in \\mathbb{R}^{+}$ which satisfies the following conditions:\r\n\r\n[b]I. [/b] $\\frac{\\sqrt a}{\\cos \\theta} + \\frac{\\sqrt a}{\\sin \\theta} >\r\n1$.\r\n\r\n[b]II.[/b] There exists $x \\in \\lbrack 1 - \\frac{\\sqrt a}{\\sin \\theta},\r\n\\frac{\\sqrt a}{\\cos \\theta} \\rbrack$ such that $\\lbrack (1 -\r\nx)\\sin \\theta - \\sqrt{a - x^2 \\cos^{2} \\theta} \\rbrack^{2} +\r\n\\lbrack x\\cos \\theta - \\sqrt{a - (1 - x)^2 \\sin^{2} \\theta}\r\n\\rbrack^{2} \\leq a$.",
