   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 239199,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 38401,
    "poster_id": 1991,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > be a natural number greater than 2. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\"  width=\"5\" height=\"12\" > is a line on a plane. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > distinct points <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" >,</span> <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107c7c8e5a64d81ed24331e510b777b7d08345b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" >,</span> …, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" > on <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\"  width=\"5\" height=\"12\" >.</span> Let the product of distances between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e86919caff4a26af2c8867c56bcd9134bfd241ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" > and the other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" > points be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f1544d77330dc5a289ad6a42beeb236b8dd70a9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" > <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\">(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f2404216e5ad3c533e1915a8563309a50f3fe06b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 1, 2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" ></span> …, <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" >)</span>. There exists a point <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" >,</span> which does not lie on <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\"  width=\"5\" height=\"12\" >,</span> on the plane. Let the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" > to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e86919caff4a26af2c8867c56bcd9134bfd241ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" > be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/1/c117e8403b3b9cf74d2f63f6627aa17c1995e3bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" > <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\">(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f2404216e5ad3c533e1915a8563309a50f3fe06b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 1, 2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" ></span> …, <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" >)</span>. Find <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a6c535fdb93a64df94d5429699a918c8761385b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n = \\sum_{i = 1}^{n} (-1)^{n-i} \\frac{c_i^2}{d_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"149\" height=\"48\" >.</span>",
    "post_canonical": "Let $n$ be a natural number greater than 2. $l$ is a line on a plane. There are $n$ distinct points $P_1$, $P_2$, …, $P_n$ on $l$. Let the product of distances between $P_i$ and the other $n-1$ points be $d_i$ ($i = 1, 2,$ …, $n$). There exists a point $Q$, which does not lie on $l$, on the plane. Let the distance from $Q$ to $P_i$ be $C_i$ ($i = 1, 2,$ …, $n$). Find $S_n = \\sum_{i = 1}^{n} (-1)^{n-i} \\frac{c_i^2}{d_i}$.",
    "username": "orl",
    "post_number": 1,
    "post_format": "bbcode",
    "category_name": "High School Olympiads",
