    "post_rendered": "For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ffd8b768c8a3ab03a57e67effaf3fa0fda167c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = 2^{r}$\"  width=\"49\" height=\"12\" > <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\">(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\"  width=\"8\" height=\"8\" ></span> is a non-negative integer), find all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767a53f43be056f9333f71e3e39f59aa0f8bca35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" > which satisfy the following condition: There exists an odd natural number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cce1bd621aff652b0983cbc94a24545e5f4bdcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" > and <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/961d336c96250f23ace9c62514783e30511c69cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" >,</span> such that <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddf2a4834539aeff224e39a201f2372535c0a958.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\mid m^{h} - 1, m \\mid n^{\\frac{m^{h}-1}{k}} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"199\" height=\"26\" >.</span>",
    "post_canonical": "For any $h = 2^{r}$ ($r$ is a non-negative integer), find all $k \\in \\mathbb{N}$ which satisfy the following condition: There exists an odd natural number $m > 1$ and $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$, such that $k \\mid m^{h} - 1, m \\mid n^{\\frac{m^{h}-1}{k}} + 1$.",
