   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 240173,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 38402,
    "poster_id": 651,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/7/13781c7822d8d63d3fc6d7ac801b685f69218ed4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^a||m^h-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" > and <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/8/758f5ae2e1fca674beb8a48b8d6874123bcf356e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^b||k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"20\" >.</span> Then <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/1/ce15c882e3b28480a1eaabda64ead2cd79ecb607.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{a-b}||\\frac{m^h-1}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"101\" height=\"39\" >,</span> so since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"8\" > divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/3/6231c4610fb0d4696f1474e7578e649b07177ae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{\\frac{m^h-1}{k}}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"23\" > there is a residue modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"8\" > of order <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/3/2237046f5f1c00594f609cf00d134a3aa492deb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{a-b+1}$\"  width=\"48\" height=\"15\" >,</span> it easily follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/3/2237046f5f1c00594f609cf00d134a3aa492deb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{a-b+1}$\"  width=\"48\" height=\"15\" > divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/0/ab0727c08c4aaa6fa119bd3fafe17851e431fd70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" > for every prime divisor of <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"8\" >,</span> and hence <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/9/5d941d422f6916407d86ce50d273b66641ddb910.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{a-b+2}|m^2-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"20\" >.</span><br>\n<br>\nBy induction on <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\"  width=\"8\" height=\"8\" >,</span> we can prove that  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/c/1dcf11b5a6e2a7a66abe9fade34828f9b50fe8a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^t||m^h-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" > iff and only iff <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/a/e4ad72ebb0fd42343e66a19244afe21da692ed50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^t||(m^2-1)2^{r-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"19\" > so we get that:<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/00393ae96f84e7e272b30c1683e5e881f81aecab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-b+2+r-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"132\" height=\"14\" > is at most <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"8\" >,</span> so from here it follows that  <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61c59b0f912dd328d0bd0d262ef0a0c49a5405b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\geq r+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"15\" >.</span> We prove this is a sufficient condition.<br>\n<br>\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/e/e5e4b29348b390ea0d6edb89704e6283a21904da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2^{r+1+t}h$\"  width=\"92\" height=\"15\" > with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"12\" > odd. Iff t is not <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\"  width=\"8\" height=\"12\" >,</span> then choose an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"8\" > such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/f/44f618707cbc7932aae905adb42395d5a2927316.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{t+2}$\"  width=\"30\" height=\"15\" > is the max power of 2 dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/b/24bcbf52b1f47f6dc6884b24824b0fbfdd4ae5b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" > and also such that <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/1/a61256f31e05c9856789d8a6d11d445e8873ab27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h|m-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" >,</span> and put <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019151d4149ad9910fe7b14de45b542a75d91000.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=m+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" >,</span> in this case everything works.<br>\n<br>\niff <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a607fd61885c014512c949fee18869690330407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=0$\"  width=\"39\" height=\"12\" >,</span> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" > be a prime of the form <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/2/9321a843ef1e24e46b008f5f8b37d69f7faf4b11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8j+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" >,</span> and such that <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/d/79d19a877bbd6262cad7534494e2ab39f234023c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h|p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" >,</span> then there exist an <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" >,</span> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f55a7827b23d850bed0d0c3bf0880b27ffcca2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" > is a multiple of <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" >,</span> so this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > works!",
    "post_canonical": "Let $2^a||m^h-1$ and $2^b||k$. Then $2^{a-b}||\\frac{m^h-1}{k}$, so since $m$ divides $n^{\\frac{m^h-1}{k}}+1$ there is a residue modulo $m$ of order $2^{a-b+1}$, it easily follows that $2^{a-b+1}$ divides $p-1$ for every prime divisor of $m$, and hence $2^{a-b+2}|m^2-1$.\r\n\r\nBy induction on $r$, we can prove that  $2^t||m^h-1$ iff and only iff $2^t||(m^2-1)2^{r-1}$ so we get that:\r\n$a-b+2+r-1$ is at most $a$, so from here it follows that  $b\\geq r+1$. We prove this is a sufficient condition.\r\n\r\nLet $k=2^{r+1+t}h$ with $h$ odd. Iff t is not $0$, then choose an $m$ such that $2^{t+2}$ is the max power of 2 dividing $m^2-1$ and also such that $h|m-1$, and put $n=m+1$, in this case everything works.\r\n\r\niff $t=0$, let $p$ be a prime of the form $8j+5$, and such that $h|p-1$, then there exist an $n$, such that $n^2+1$ is a multiple of $p$, so this $n$ works!",
